            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for to have someone sent for, then the Hindi for a life."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: मालिश",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मालिश — māliś — \"a massage; a rub\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रोज़ की मालिश से दादी के घुटनों का दर्द कम हो गया। roz kī māliś se dādī ke ghuṭnoṁ kā dard kam ho gayā. With a daily massage, the pain in my grandmother's knees eased."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मालिश (māliś) is usually traced to Persian mālish, \"rubbing\", the noun of the Persian verb for \"to rub\". māliś karnā is to massage; malnā, \"to rub in\", is a separate, inherited word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
